-------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOLTS — fastener dimension tables
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Components: ISO 4762 / DIN 912 socket-head cap screw dimensions
            (crates/onecad-library/src/tables/iso4762.rs,
             worker/src/ops/FastenerTables.cpp::iso4762_table())
            data/hex_socket.blt, class "hexsocketheadcap"
            Retrieved 2026-08-12

            (ISO 4014, ISO 4017, ISO 4032 and ISO 7089 tables were also
            transcribed from BOLTS and have since been REMOVED along with
            their generators. No BOLTS-derived data from those classes
            remains in the tree; the entries are dropped here rather than
            kept as a claim about data that is not shipped.)

Source:     BOLTS — Open Library of Technical Specifications
            https://github.com/boltsparts/BOLTS_archive

Author:     Johannes Reinhardt <jreinhardt@ist-dein-freund.de>

License:    GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
            (LGPL-2.1+), per each file's own header. Full text:
            https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-2.1.html

Notes:      Dimension values (M2–M12 where the standard defines them)
            transcribed into two independent, purpose-specific
            representations — Rust metadata tables
            (onecad-library::tables) and C++ worker generator tables
            (FastenerTables.cpp) — per this project's architecture
            (generators are built-in/versioned in the worker; the library
            crate serves authoring/metadata, not geometry). Neither copy
            embeds BOLTS source code, only the published dimension data.
            The repository's GitHub-reported top-level license (GPL-3.0)
            is a whole-repo default; the specific data files used here
            carry their own LGPL 2.1+ headers, which is the license that
            applies to this data.

            The shipped ISO 4762 values are verbatim from the source. (A
            correction was carried against BOLTS' ISO 7089 M10 inner
            diameter — 10.0 mm there, 10.5 mm in ISO 7089 and DIN 125 A —
            for as long as that table shipped; it no longer does.)

